# ts-route-fix site configuration
#
# FORMAT (pipe-delimited, 5 fields):
#   SITE_NAME | SEARCH_DOMAINS | LOCAL_IP_PREFIX | TS_REMOVE_ROUTES | GW_ADD_ROUTES
#
# Field details:
#   SITE_NAME        Identifier shown in log output
#   SEARCH_DOMAINS   Comma-separated strings matched against /etc/resolv.conf "search" line
#   LOCAL_IP_PREFIX  Comma-separated IP prefixes used as fallback detection (e.g. "10.0.1.")
#   TS_REMOVE_ROUTES Comma-separated CIDRs to delete from the Tailscale interface
#   GW_ADD_ROUTES    Comma-separated CIDRs to re-add via the local gateway (can be empty)
#
# Detection order:
#   1. SEARCH_DOMAINS match (preferred — DNS config changes as soon as you connect)
#   2. LOCAL_IP_PREFIX match (fallback — check actual IP address)
#
# Behavior:
#   Matched site:  TS_REMOVE_ROUTES are deleted from Tailscale; GW_ADD_ROUTES are
#                  added via the local default gateway.
#   Other sites:   Their GW_ADD_ROUTES are cleaned up (removes stale entries from
#                  previous locations).
#   No match:      Script reports EXTERNAL, still cleans up all GW_ADD_ROUTES.
#
# Notes:
#   - Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored
#   - Whitespace around | is included in field values — avoid padding
#   - CIDR operations are idempotent; missing routes are silently skipped
#
# ── Examples ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Routes removed from Tailscale and re-added via the local gateway:
# site1|site1.example.com|192.168.1.|192.168.1.0/24,192.168.2.0/24|192.168.1.0/24,192.168.2.0/24

# Routes removed from Tailscale only (directly-connected; no explicit GW add needed):
# site2|site2.example.com|10.1.0.|10.1.0.0/24,10.1.1.0/24,10.1.2.0/24|

# Multiple subnets and multiple detection domains (comma-separated within each field):
# site3|site3.example.com,site3.example.internal|172.16.0.|172.16.0.0/24,172.16.1.0/24,172.16.2.0/24,172.16.3.0/24|172.16.0.0/24,172.16.1.0/24,172.16.2.0/24,172.16.3.0/24

# Detection by IP prefix only (no distinctive search domain):
# site4||10.10.5.|10.10.5.0/24,10.10.6.0/24|10.10.5.0/24,10.10.6.0/24
